User has sent a report about their VPN disconnecting and won't reconnect.

We do first a remote desktop to check the users VPN settings.
Trying to click connect gives this error message:

VPN connection failed - Stale DNS entries are blocking the tunnel.
Open the terminal and run "ipconfig/flushdns" to clear the DNS cache first.

After running the command, restart the PC to apply the changes.

We need to ask the user for the password to their device and log back in to see whether the problem still persist.

After logging in and giving the connect VPN button another attempt, it connects and is working again.

Ticket closed.
